# Print-in-place fit proof for the sweetheart-hamster clamshell locket.
# `fitcheck` intersects the two halves in the FLAT print pose — the pose CI
# actually slices — and it must render EMPTY: the halves clear, so the locket
# prints as two bodies bridged only by the hinge web, not welded shut.
# v0.1 shipped this check against the CLOSED pose (fold=90), which is exactly
# why the flat-pose weld passed green; v0.2 tests the sliced pose.
# `fitcheck_neg` drops the fold axis below the model top (the v0.1 geometry),
# so the two halves overlap and the intersection MUST interfere — the mandatory
# negative control proving the empty check can actually fail. (Separability is
# additionally gated by ci.fusecheck; this proves boolean clearance.)
fitcheck      empty
fitcheck_neg  interferes
